## Why

The Overview showed three lists under "What is moving", each chosen by its own rule: the newest drafts, a velocity band and the newest tensions. Below them sat all-time corpus totals and a log feed. To a gentells.com member the page opened on the team's review queue, and the log feed stayed empty because members can't read the logs.

## The Overview

It answers one question for the team and a member alike: what moved this week.

- **This week**: "61 new insights in all sectors and all regions, strongest first." The sector and the region are words in that sentence: click one to choose. They set the same `topic` and `region` filters Insights and Patterns carry, so the choice follows you there. The six strongest insights follow, each with what it rests on in words ("72 signals, 1 pattern") in place of a bare score.
- **Rising**: patterns mentioned more this week than the week before, as the two counts ("31 this week, 22 the week before"), not as a percentage. Hidden until the pipeline has counted the patterns.
- **Ask about this week**: two questions built from the items above. A click opens Ask with the question typed in but not sent, so a member's daily questions are still theirs to spend.
- **For the team**: "Needs you" stays first, and the draft list is now one line in it ("9 insights were drafted in the last 24 hours", with a link to read the drafts). The corpus (topics, regions, Live activity) moved into the machine fold.
- **Gone from the page**: Insight drafts, Accelerating, Tensions (still on the Graph page), and the open corpus section.
- **For a member**: no fold; one line instead, "The Observatory read N signals in the last 24 hours, and M since it began". The page no longer requests the team's data (workers, budget, supervisor, reports, site trends) for a member; the server refused those requests every ten seconds.

## Insights

The default sort is now by week: This week, Last week and Earlier, each with a count, strongest first within each week. Sorted by date alone, a three-signal draft from this morning stood above the 70-signal readings of the day before. "Newest" and "Strongest of all" remain as choices.

## Merge with the pipeline

This reads the new `overview-home` shape from the pipeline change. Merge the pipeline first, then this one soon after.

## Checked

- `e2e/overview.spec.js`, 9 new tests:
  - the week, strongest first, with what each insight rests on;
  - rising as counts;
  - the sector choice narrows the week, and the links carry it;
  - the Ask question arrives typed and not sent;
  - Needs you with the drafts line;
  - the corpus inside the fold;
  - the member view, with none of the team's requests sent;
  - Insights grouped by week;
  - Newest still available.
- Mutation check: five guards undone one at a time, and each turns a test red:
  - the default sort back to Newest;
  - the team's requests sent for a member;
  - the Ask question ignored;
  - the filter not sent;
  - the fold shown to a member.
- Full e2e: 60 of 60. The lint ratchet is unchanged (at its ceiling), and the build passes.
- Browser: walked on a local stack holding this week's 61 real insights, as the team and as a member signed in through the stand-in gentells.com.
